{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28268 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Ajugalide C is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ajugalide C acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Quercitrin-7-olate, Armepavine, and romidepsin, all of which are themselves targets of CCRF-HSB-2. This implies that the High-affinity choline transporter is a downstream effector of these compounds, which in turn are influenced by Ajugalide C. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Ajugalide C modulates the activity of CCRF-HSB-2, which then affects the choline transporter. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, albeit indirect, relationship, suggesting that the choline transporter is a key downstream target in the signaling cascade initiated by Ajugalide C. This connection underscores the role of CCRF-HSB-2 as a central mediator in the interaction between Ajugalide C and the choline transporter.",
